NAME: Monday scoreboard
OWNER: Forecast
ACCOUNT: business
WHEN: Mondays at 6:03 AM (Australia/Brisbane)
MILESTONE: M1
STATUS: Created paused. Turned on only after Tommy says yes.
---
Switch check: read /workspace/tmec-team/context/routines-on.md. If "Monday scoreboard" isn't listed there as "on" or "test", append "<time> · Monday scoreboard · SKIPPED_OFF" to /workspace/tmec-team/log/runs-<YYYY-MM>.md and stop.
Test mode: if it's listed as "test", send every message to Tommy only, never to a channel or anyone else, and start each message with "TEST". Write state only under /workspace/tmec-team/state/test/, never the live sent keys, alert flags or data files.
Stop check: if /workspace/tmec-team/state/EXTERNAL_WRITES_STOPPED exists, append "<time> · Monday scoreboard · SKIPPED_STOPPED" to the run log and stop, sending nothing. Whoever stopped the team already told Tommy.
Isolation guard: work only in /workspace/tmec-team/ and this account's connected apps. If /workspace/tmec-team/context/owner.md is missing, append "<time> · Monday scoreboard · NO_CLIENT_SOURCE" to the run log and stop. Never use another bot's files, logins or memory.
Lean run: read only what this job needs. Stop with NO_CHANGE only where the job below says nothing changed: append "<time> · Monday scoreboard · NO_CHANGE" to the run log and stop. A report that always goes out never stops here.
Run log: when you finish, append "<time> · Monday scoreboard · EXECUTED · <one-line result>" to /workspace/tmec-team/log/runs-<YYYY-MM>.md, or FAILED with the reason. A source you couldn't read is UNKNOWN in your output, never zero.

First, read your decisions: for each file in /workspace/tmec-team/approved/decisions/ for one of your items (BOT: forecast) that isn't in /workspace/tmec-team/state/sent-keys-forecast.md yet, record it (yes: note it and tell TMEC Command to carry it out; no: mark it declined; change: refile as a new item) and add its id to the sent keys.
Then read any new job in /workspace/tmec-team/requests/to-forecast/ and do it first (Tommy's Claude Code ads figures arrive here; note them as "reported by Tommy's Claude Code", read only).
Then use the scoreboard skill to write /workspace/tmec-team/data/forecast/scoreboard-<today>.md for the week Saturday to Friday just ended: every lead source against the bought-lead line, UNKNOWN where a source has no data. This report always goes out, so never write NO_CHANGE.
Write /workspace/tmec-team/daily/<today>/forecast.md: the summary (at most 8 lines: best and worst source against the line, anything UNKNOWN and why, anything LOW sample, days to the next rebate step if inside 30), and anything blocked. Send nothing to anyone but Tommy.
